  "chapter": 773,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 71 Chapter 773\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8145, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the executive law, in relation to information on\n        state boards\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would amend Executive Law by  requiring  the  Commis-\nsioner  of  the  Office  of  General  Services to compile and maintain a\ncompilation of State boards. The legislation would  also  require  State\nagencies  to  provide  annual  updates  on  membership, costs, and other\ninformation about State boards to the  Commissioner  of  the  Office  of\nGeneral  Services.   Finally, the bill would require the Commissioner of\nthe Office of General Services to update the Legislature and the  Gover-\nnor  on  the  status of the compilation of the State boards. The goal of\nthe legislation is to create a database which can  improve  transparency\nand  assist  government  in  eliminating  duplicative  or nonfunctioning\nboards while ensuring that the public is aware of the boards  in  exist-\nence. I support increasing transparency across State government.\n \n  However,  this legislation required several amendments before it could\nbe signed into law. The Legislature has agreed to these  changes,  which\nensure  that  the boards being captured have an important policy making,\nrather than purely advisory, function. The changes require  each  agency\nto  post the following: the language creating the board (be it by execu-\ntive order, law or other legal basis); the size and  current  membership\nalong with qualifications of the board; eligibility for payment or other\ncompensation  for  duties;  and  any other information deemed necessary.\nFinally, the effective date for implementation was moved to allow  agen-\ncies  to better prepare. These changes will help ensure that the goal of\ntransparency is met to allow the public access to the  information  most\nrelevant to the work of government.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
